{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfBSEJwShtoVQmDWx19fR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The campaign is finished and submitted: my pick is **index 2 (Ag 0.62 / Sb 0.38)**, which gave the highest EQE I measured at 2.1 eV, about **1.03 %**.\n\n| Index | Ag : Sb | EQE (%) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2 | 0.62 : 0.38 | 1.03 |\n| 5 | 0.50 : 0.50 | 0.064 |\n| 16 | 0.18 : 0.82 | about 0 (−0.001) |\n\n- **Budget:** I used all 3 merit measurements and 4 of the 5 XRD scans.\n- **XRD:** The Ag-rich end shows metallic Ag plus an Ag–Sb oxide phase. Toward the Sb-rich end, peaks from an Sb6O13-type antimony oxide get stronger. That oxide probably absorbs little light at 2.1 eV, which fits the EQE falling as Sb increases.\n- **Main caveat:** EQE was still rising steeply toward the Ag-rich end. So index 0 or 1 (Ag 0.67 or 0.63) could be better than index 2, but I had no merit measurements left to test them. If you get more budget, measure index 1 first, then index 0."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":555,"cache_read_input_tokens":9474,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":555},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5a46ea20-a77d-4a81-ac4e-3c11189bf2a8","uuid":"5f0bf2c4-550a-4f26-a6c7-5b7a92e2bc59","timestamp":"2026-09-18T19:12:18.276Z","request_id":"req_011CfBSEJUA8bPhknp8oH8xz"}
